# Clean hotfix / dirty-tree ships

**Goal:** messy prompts still produce a small, isolated ship. Do not invent stash/worktree theater for a 1–6 file polish.

## Default path (use this most of the time)

1. Edit **only** files required for the ask.
2. `git add -- <those paths>` (never `git add -A`).
3. `git diff --cached` — if anything unrelated appears, unstage and stop.
4. Commit / push only when asked.

Dirty tree is normal here. Unrelated WIP can stay unstaged.

## When `app.py` is dirty

| Need | Path |
|------|------|
| No `app.py` change | Default path above. Ignore dirty `app.py`. |
| One line / one hunk (cache `?v=`, meta, header) | Backup → `git checkout HEAD -- app.py` → edit → stage that hunk → commit → restore backup. Prefer `_scratch/app.py.wip_backup_*`. |
| Multi-hunk / tangled `app.py` | Worktree or stash — see escalation. |

```powershell
Copy-Item app.py _scratch\app.py.wip_backup_hotfix -Force
git checkout HEAD -- app.py
# edit the one hunk
git add -- app.py
git diff --cached -- app.py   # must be only that hunk
# commit when asked
Copy-Item _scratch\app.py.wip_backup_hotfix app.py -Force
```

## Escalation (worktree / stash) — only if

- The ship **requires** large or tangled `app.py` edits that cannot be isolated as one hunk, **or**
- Pre-push / hooks cannot run sanely from the main dirty tree.

Then: worktree from `origin/master`, or tracked-only stash. Prefer worktree over stash when both are viable.

Do **not** open a worktree for CSS-only, markdown-only, PNG-only, or one-line cache busts.

## Scope

- No drive-by owners/geo/premium/spark/API work.
- Follow-up ideas → separate commit or ask first.
- Scratch: `_scratch/`, not root `_smoke_*` / `_patch_*` / `_tmp_*`.

## Anti-patterns

- Patching polish into mega-dirty `app.py`, then trying to isolate at push time
- Worktree/stash as the **first** move for every hotfix
- Multitask agents editing the same dirty `app.py` without a clean base
- Bundling unrelated WIP into a UI/OG polish push
